A fairly successful way to find email addresses is
to search for the author's posting name separated by
periods, like author:simon.de.vet, using google
groups search feature, find the message ID, then
find the message on some other service by message ID
search, or else guess the missing part of the email
address from what Google Groups leaves intact.

Unfortunately, not too many other services than
Google Groups keep archives three years deep, so
finding a clear email address that far back is
"interesting" when Google Groups insists on munging
the email address.

